  "rewritten_text": "Get up! What are you doing? I opened my eyes, confused about my surroundings. It was past sunrise, and I had been fast asleep. Pap stood over me, looking grumpy and ill. He asked what I was doing with the gun. Realizing he did not remember his actions from the night before, I told him someone had tried to break in, so I was waiting for them. He asked why I had not woken him, and I explained that I could not move him. He told me to stop talking and go check the fishing lines for breakfast, promising to follow shortly. He unlocked the door, and I headed up the riverbank. I noticed branches and bark floating by, signaling that the river was rising. I thought about how the June rise usually brought good luck, as logs and firewood would drift down for me to catch and sell. I walked along the bank, watching for Pap and any useful debris. Suddenly, I spotted a beautiful canoe, about fourteen feet long, floating by. I dove into the water and swam out to it. I expected someone to be hiding inside to play a trick, but it was empty. I paddled it to shore, thinking Pap would be pleased with a ten-dollar find. However, he was not around, so I decided to hide the boat in a vine-covered creek. I realized this was my chance to escape by river instead of running away on foot. I quickly hid the canoe, constantly worried that Pap might appear. After securing it, I peeked through the willows and saw him down the path, aiming his gun at a bird."
}

