parts.text:
{
  "request_id": "48b4c27e404a2f0aec4600c0",
  "rewritten_text": "Reviewing the terrible list of my transgressions, I struggle to accept that I am the same being who once harbored lofty dreams of virtue and grace. Yet it is true; the fallen angel transforms into a spiteful demon. Even that adversary of the divine had companions in his exile, whereas I remain solitary. You, who claim friendship with Frankenstein, seem aware of my offenses and his tragedies. However, his account could not capture the endless months of agony I suffered while consumed by futile rage. In ruining his prospects, I found no fulfillment for my own longings. I perpetually craved affection and companionship, only to be rejected. Was this not unfair? Am I the sole villain when humanity wronged me? Why is Felix not condemned for casting his friend away with disdain? Why is the peasant not reviled for attacking the one who saved his child? They are considered righteous, while I, abandoned and wretched, am viewed as a monstrosity fit only for abuse. The memory of such inequity still inflames my blood. It is true that I am a villain. I have slaughtered the beautiful and the defenseless; I have strangled the innocent in their sleep and ended the life of one who never harmed a soul. I have condemned my creator, the finest of men, to despair, pursuing him until his final ruin. He lies there, pale and lifeless. Your hatred for me cannot match the loathing I feel for myself. I gaze upon the hands that committed these acts and contemplate the mind that devised them, yearning for the moment when I am no longer haunted by these memories. Do not fear further harm from me. My task is nearly finished. No more lives are required to conclude my existence; only my own death is necessary. I will not hesitate to make this sacrifice. I shall depart your ship on the ice raft that carried me here and travel to the furthest north. There, I will build my funeral pyre and burn this wretched body to ashes, ensuring that no curious soul can ever study my remains to replicate such a creature as I have been."
}

