  "request_id": "2428ec65ec0e75c6b6bf1441",
  "rewritten_text": "Well, you rascal, the elderly woman exclaimed as he walked in, why have you stayed away so long? My dear Lady Clem, I am constantly occupied, Lord Arthur replied with a smile. I assume you mean you spend your days with Miss Sybil Merton, shopping for clothes and whispering sweet nothings? I fail to see why everyone makes such a spectacle of marriage. In my youth, we never engaged in public displays of affection. I promise I have not seen Sybil in a full day, Lady Clem. As far as I can tell, she is entirely devoted to her dressmakers. Naturally; that is why you visit a plain old woman like me. I am surprised you men do not learn from experience. Men once acted foolishly for my sake, and now I am merely a rheumatic invalid with a wig and a sour disposition. If not for Lady Jansen sending me scandalous French novels, I would be bored to tears. Physicians are useless, save for collecting fees; they cannot even remedy my indigestion. I have brought you a remedy for that, Lady Clem, Lord Arthur said seriously. It is a remarkable invention from America. I doubt I would care for American gadgets, Arthur. I recently read some American fiction, and it was utter nonsense. This is quite practical, I assure you! You must promise to use it, Lord Arthur insisted, producing a small box from his pocket. The box is lovely, Arthur. Is it truly a gift? How kind. And this is the medicine? It resembles a candy. I shall try it immediately. Good heavens, Lady Clem! Lord Arthur exclaimed, seizing her hand. You must not. It is a homeopathic remedy, and taking it without symptoms could be dangerous. Wait for an attack, and then use it. You will be amazed by the effect. I would prefer to take it now, Lady Clementina said, examining the transparent capsule containing a bubble of liquid aconitine. I am certain it is delightful. Though I despise doctors, I adore medicine. Very well, I shall save it for my next episode. And when might that occur? Lord Arthur inquired anxiously."
}

