  "rewritten_text": "Heavily armored knights and horses were limited in speed. With the ground firm and free of snow or mud, they might manage a seven-mile pace, requiring a few horse changes. They should arrive around six, while daylight remained, spotting the white cloth on my arm so I could assume command. We would quickly surround the prison and liberate the king. It promised to be a dramatic spectacle, though I would have preferred the theatricality of high noon. To bolster my options, I considered revealing my identity to former acquaintances to resolve our predicament without the knights. However, the risk required caution. I needed to acquire fine clothing gradually, purchasing increasingly luxurious garments at distant shops until I reached silk and velvet. I began my task, but the plan collapsed instantly. Turning a corner, I encountered one of our slaves with a watchman. My cough drew a piercing look from him, as if he recognized the sound. I ducked into a shop, feigning interest in merchandise while watching them confer at the entrance. Deciding to escape through the rear, I told the shopkeeper I was an undercover officer hunting a fugitive. I claimed my partner was outside with a captured murderer and asked her to tell him to move to the far end of the alley to intercept the suspect once I flushed him out. Eager to see a notorious criminal, she hurried off to deliver the message."
}

