  "rewritten_text": "What is wrong? Oliver asked. Hush, the Dodger replied. Do you see that old man at the book stall? The gentleman across the street? Oliver asked. Yes, I see him. He will do, the Dodger said. A perfect target, Charley Bates added. Oliver looked at them in surprise, but they did not let him ask questions. The two boys crept across the road and slipped behind the man. Oliver followed a few steps, then stopped in silent amazement, unsure whether to move forward or turn back. The gentleman looked very respectable, with powdered hair and gold spectacles. He wore a green coat with a velvet collar, white trousers, and carried a bamboo cane. He had picked up a book and was reading it as intently as if he were in his own study. He seemed completely lost in the text, unaware of the street or the boys nearby. Oliver watched in horror as the Dodger reached into the man's pocket, pulled out a handkerchief, and handed it to Charley Bates. Then, both boys sprinted around the corner. Suddenly, the truth about the handkerchiefs, watches, and jewels became clear to Oliver. Terrified, he felt as though he were burning up. Confused and scared, he turned and ran as fast as he could. This all happened in a minute. As Oliver started running, the old man reached for his pocket, realized his handkerchief was gone, and turned around. Seeing the boy sprinting away, he assumed Oliver was the thief. He shouted Stop thief! at the top of his lungs and chased after him, still holding his book."
}

