  "rewritten_text": "I handed the paper back and said, \"I am still just as confused. Even if the jewels of Golconda were my reward for solving this puzzle, I am certain I could never earn them.\" Legrand replied, \"The solution is not as difficult as it first appears. These symbols are clearly a code, but knowing Kidd, I doubted he could create anything truly complex. I assumed it was a simple cipher that would seem impossible to an uneducated sailor without the key.\" \"And you actually solved it?\" I asked. \"Easily,\" he said. \"I have solved far more difficult ones. My mind is naturally drawn to such riddles, and I doubt there is any puzzle human intelligence can create that it cannot also solve. Once I had the characters, the meaning was simple to find. In any secret writing, the first step is identifying the language, as the method of solving depends on the specific tongue. Usually, you must test different languages based on probability until you find the right one. However, the signature here made it clear. The pun on the name 'Kidd' only works in English. Otherwise, I would have started with Spanish or French, as those would be common for a pirate. Because of that, I assumed the code was in English. Notice there are no spaces between the words. If there were, the task would be much easier. I would have analyzed the short words first, and if a single-letter word like 'a' or 'I' appeared, the solution would be certain. Since there are no divisions, my first step was to identify which letters appeared most and least frequently."
}

