parts.text:
{
  "request_id": "e81eae044f177b1a136bcff9",
  "rewritten_text": "The little man’s body was unusually broad, giving him a comical, round appearance. His feet were hidden, though a strange, hard substance occasionally poked through a hole in the bottom of his hat. His hands were massive. He had gray hair tied in a ponytail, a long, crooked, red nose, and sharp, bright eyes. His cheeks and chin were wrinkled but puffy, and he appeared to have no ears at all. He wore a loose sky-blue satin coat with matching tight breeches buckled at the knees, a bright yellow vest, and a white cap tilted jauntily. A large, blood-red silk handkerchief was tied in a fancy, oversized bow around his neck. Once he descended to about one hundred feet above the ground, the man grew nervous and seemed unwilling to land. He struggled to toss sand from a canvas bag, causing his craft to hover. Agitated, he pulled a large leather wallet from his pocket, weighed it with surprise, and opened it to retrieve a thick letter sealed with red wax and tied with red tape. He dropped it right at the feet of the mayor, Superbus Von Underduk. As the mayor bent to pick it up, the flustered traveler prepared to leave. To rise again, he dropped half a dozen bags of ballast. They landed directly on the mayor, rolling him over twenty-one times in front of everyone in Rotterdam. Naturally, the mayor did not intend to let this insult go unpunished."
}

