parts.text:
{
  "request_id": "70c2640f797465051a08077a",
  "rewritten_text": "Shortly after noon, the boys borrowed a small boat from an absent owner and set off. Several miles past Cave Hollow, Tom pointed to a landslide on the bluff. He explained it was a landmark and steered them to the shore. Tom told Huck the cave entrance was nearby, but Huck could not find it. Tom walked into a thicket of bushes and revealed the opening. He told Huck to keep it a secret, noting that they would form a gang with Joe Harper and Ben Rogers. Tom Sawyer’s Gang, he declared, sounded impressive. Huck asked who they would rob, and Tom explained they would waylay people. When Huck asked if they would kill them, Tom said they would hold them for ransom. He explained that a ransom is money collected from friends, and if it is not paid after a year, the captives are killed. He added that women are never killed, only held captive, and that they eventually fall in love with the robbers because of their polite manners. Huck agreed that being a robber sounded better than being a pirate because it was closer to home. The boys then entered the cave, with Tom leading the way. They reached the end of the tunnel, tied their kite strings to a rock, and continued inside."
}

