parts.text:
{
  "request_id": "95896dfacd67aa9d7b845bd4",
  "rewritten_text": "“Everyone lives that way, Huck.” “Tom, it makes no difference. I am not everyone, and I cannot endure it. Being confined is dreadful. Food comes too easily, so I have no appetite for it. I must ask permission to fish, to swim, to do anything at all. I had to speak so politely that it offered no comfort; I had to retreat to the attic to vent my frustrations daily just to feel like myself, or I would have perished. The widow forbade me from smoking, yelling, yawning, stretching, or scratching in public.” [He added with a surge of annoyance] “And confound it, she prayed constantly! I never encountered such a woman. I had to leave, Tom; I simply had to. Furthermore, school is starting, and I would have been forced to attend. I would not tolerate that. Listen, Tom, being wealthy is not as wonderful as people claim. It is nothing but constant worry and toil, making one wish they were dead. These clothes and this barrel suit me, and I will never abandon them. I would never have faced this trouble if not for that money. Take my share along with yours, give me a dime occasionally—not often, because I do not care for things unless they are difficult to obtain—and please convince the widow to let me be.” “Oh, Huck, you know I cannot do that. It is not fair, and if you try this life a little longer, you will grow to enjoy it.” “Enjoy it! Yes, the way I would enjoy sitting on a hot stove. No, Tom, I will not be rich, and I will not live in those stifling houses. I prefer the woods, the river, and my barrel, and I am staying with them. Confound it! Just as we had secured guns and a cave, ready to begin our robberies, this foolishness has to ruin everything!” Tom saw his chance. “Listen, Huck, being rich will not stop me from becoming a robber.” “No! Oh, goodness; are you truly serious, Tom?” “As serious as I am sitting here. But Huck, we cannot allow you into the gang unless you are respectable.” Huck’s joy vanished. “You cannot let me in, Tom?”"
}

