parts.text:
{
  "request_id": "d2d784abfd902100eff4f000",
  "rewritten_text": "He emerged silently from the paneling, a malicious grin twisting his withered lips, while the moon obscured itself behind a cloud as he crept past the expansive bay window, which displayed his family crest alongside that of his slain wife in blue and gold. He drifted forward like a malevolent specter, the shadows themselves appearing to recoil from his presence. Pausing briefly at a distant sound, he realized it was merely a dog barking at the Red Farm, so he continued, whispering archaic oaths and waving his corroded blade through the night. Upon reaching the hallway leading to Washington’s chamber, he halted, his grey hair whipping in the wind and his burial shroud swirling into eerie shapes. As the clock chimed the quarter-hour, he sensed his moment had arrived. He let out a soft laugh and rounded the corner, only to recoil instantly with a cry of alarm, burying his pale face in his skeletal hands. Before him stood a terrifying apparition, still as stone and grotesque as a fever dream. Its skull was polished and hairless, its face bloated and pallid, frozen in a permanent, mocking sneer. Crimson light poured from its eyes, its mouth resembled a fiery abyss, and a shroud similar to his own draped its massive frame. A placard hung upon its chest, covered in ancient, cryptic script—perhaps a list of transgressions or a ledger of sins—while its right hand brandished a shining blade. Having never encountered a spirit before, he was understandably terrified. After one frantic look, he retreated, stumbling over his own winding-sheet and accidentally dropping his dagger into the Minister’s boots, where the butler discovered it the next day. Safely back in his room, he collapsed onto his bed and pulled the covers over his head. Eventually, his courageous spirit returned, and he resolved to confront the other ghost at daybreak. As dawn painted the hills in silver, he ventured back to the site of the encounter, reasoning that two ghosts were superior to one and that, with this new ally, he might finally overcome the twins."
}

