parts.text:
{
  "request_id": "0dfd8832cf70116b4c672191",
  "rewritten_text": "Recent reports from Rotterdam suggest the city is gripped by intense intellectual fervor. Extraordinary and unprecedented events have occurred there, defying all established theories and surely throwing European scientific and astronomical circles into complete chaos. On an unspecified date, a massive throng gathered in the Exchange square of Rotterdam. The weather was unseasonably warm and still, with the crowd enjoying occasional brief showers from scattered white clouds. Around midday, however, a sudden stir rippled through the assembly. A cacophony of voices erupted, and instantly, ten thousand faces turned skyward, ten thousand pipes dropped from ten thousand mouths, and a roar akin to Niagara Falls echoed throughout the city. The cause of this commotion was soon clear. Emerging from behind a cloud into the clear blue sky was a strange, solid, and oddly constructed object that baffled the gaping citizens below. What was it, and what did it signify? Nobody, including the burgomaster Mynheer Superbus Von Underduk, had any explanation. Lacking a better response, everyone replaced their pipes, squinted upward at the phenomenon, and paced about, grunting and puffing in contemplation. Meanwhile, the object descended steadily toward the city, drawing more smoke and curiosity. Within minutes, it was close enough to identify: it was a balloon, though unlike any ever witnessed in Rotterdam before."
}

