  "request_id": "21ae537b5bafdfd0e9363f0d",
  "rewritten_text": "Sydney Carton paused in the street, uncertain of his next move. \"Tellson's bank at nine,\" he mused. \"Should I make an appearance in the meantime? Yes, it is a wise precaution for these people to know I am here.\" He paced the darkening street, weighing the consequences of his decision. Convinced of his plan, he headed toward Saint Antoine. Defarge had mentioned running a wine shop in that district, and Carton found it easily without asking for directions. After locating the shop, he ate at a nearby cafe and fell into a deep sleep. For the first time in years, he had avoided strong spirits, having poured his brandy away the night before. He woke at seven, refreshed, and returned to the streets. Before reaching Saint Antoine, he stopped at a shop window to adjust his cravat, collar, and messy hair. He then entered Defarge's shop. Only Jacques Three was there, drinking at the counter with the Defarges and The Vengeance. Carton sat down and ordered a small wine in broken French. Madame Defarge glanced at him, then studied him more intently before approaching to confirm his order. He repeated it. \"English?\" she asked, raising her eyebrows. He looked at her as if struggling to process the language, then replied with a heavy foreign accent."
}

