parts.text:
{
  "request_id": "2f8e9755420d90d9c7e831f4",
  "rewritten_text": "Well, you rascal, the old lady exclaimed as he entered, why have you stayed away so long? My dear Lady Clem, I never have a moment to myself, Lord Arthur replied with a smile. I suppose you mean you spend your days with Miss Sybil Merton, shopping and talking nonsense? I cannot understand why people make such a fuss about marriage. In my day, we never acted so affectionate in public or private. I assure you I have not seen Sybil for twenty-four hours, Lady Clem. As far as I can tell, she belongs entirely to her dressmakers. Of course; that is the only reason you visit an ugly old woman like me. I wonder you men do not take warning. People once did foolish things for me, and now I am just a poor, grumpy woman with aches and pains. If it were not for Lady Jansen, who sends me the latest French novels, I do not think I could get through the day. Doctors are useless, except for taking one's money. They cannot even cure my heartburn. I have brought you a cure for that, Lady Clem, Lord Arthur said seriously. It is a wonderful thing, invented by an American. I do not think I like American inventions, Arthur. I am quite sure I do not. I read some American novels lately, and they were nonsense. Oh, but there is no nonsense about this, Lady Clem! I assure you it is a perfect cure. You must promise to try it. Lord Arthur took a small box from his pocket and handed it to her. Well, the box is charming, Arthur. Is it really a gift? That is very sweet of you. And is this the wonderful medicine? It looks like a candy. I will take it at once. Good heavens, Lady Clem! Lord Arthur cried, grabbing her hand. You must not do that. It is a homeopathic medicine, and if you take it without having heartburn, it could do you great harm. Wait until you have an attack, and take it then. You will be amazed at the result. I would like to take it now, Lady Clementina said, holding the small transparent capsule up to the light. I am sure it is delicious. The truth is, although I hate doctors, I love medicine. However, I will keep it until my next attack. And when will that be? Lord Arthur asked eagerly."
}

