parts.text:
{
  "request_id": "0ee511cab3f4f71789c0cec0",
  "rewritten_text": "They are aware of his cleverness; he will be sent away for good. They will surely give the Artful a life sentence. What do you mean by lagging and a lifer? asked Mr. Bolter. Why speak in such a way to me; why not use plain language I can understand? Fagin prepared to explain these slang terms, which meant transportation for life, but the conversation was interrupted by Master Bates, who entered with his hands in his pockets and a look of mock misery on his face. It is all over, Fagin, Charley announced after being introduced to his new associate. What do you mean? They have located the owner of the snuffbox; others are coming to identify him, and the Artful is definitely being shipped off, Master Bates replied. I need a full mourning outfit and a hatband to visit him before he departs. To think of Jack Dawkins—the great Dodger—being sent away for a cheap, insignificant snuffbox! I expected him to go for a gold watch and chain at the very least. Why did he not rob a wealthy man of all his valuables and go abroad like a gentleman, rather than a common thief without honor or glory? Expressing his sympathy for his friend, Master Bates slumped into a chair, looking dejected. Why do you say he lacks honor or glory? Fagin snapped, glaring at his pupil. Was he not always the leader among you? Is there any one of you who could match his skill? Not one, Master Bates answered, his voice thick with sorrow. Then why are you complaining? Fagin demanded. Because it will not be on the record, Charley retorted, his grief turning into defiance; because it cannot be included in the indictment; because no one will ever know his true capabilities. How will he appear in the Newgate Calendar? Perhaps he will not be mentioned at all. Oh, what a terrible blow! Ha! ha! Fagin laughed, gesturing toward Mr. Bolter while shaking with a palsy-like tremor; observe the pride they take in their craft, my dear."
}

