parts.text:
{
  "request_id": "cd538e03bbf446386c2f0fee",
  "rewritten_text": "The surrounding oaks sheltered a colony of nightingales—I am transported back there now; young Idris, in the bloom of her youth, stands beside me—recall that I am merely twenty-two, and my beloved has seen barely seventeen summers. The river, bloated by autumn storms, flooded the lowlands, and Adrian was occupied in his preferred vessel with the perilous sport of snapping the highest branch from a sunken oak. Do you tire of existence, Adrian, that you toy so recklessly with peril? He secured his trophy and navigated the deluge; we watched him with anxious eyes, but the current swept him away, forcing him to dock downstream and travel a long path to rejoin us. He is safe, Idris remarked as he jumped ashore, brandishing the branch in triumph; we shall await him here. We remained alone; the sun had vanished, the nightingales commenced their melody, and the evening star glowed brightly within the lingering western light. My angelic companion gazed at that lovely symbol with her blue eyes. How the light flickers, she observed, as if it were the star’s own vitality. Its unsteady radiance suggests that its existence, much like our own, is uncertain; I believe it fears and loves. Do not study the star, my dear, selfless friend, I implored, nor seek love in its shivering beams; ignore distant spheres and mere fantasies of emotion. I have remained quiet for too long; I have yearned to speak to you, to surrender my soul and my entire being to your care. If you must look at the star, let its eternal glow plead my case; let it serve as my silent witness—love is to me what light is to that star; as long as it remains unextinguished, I shall love you. The ecstasy of that instant must remain hidden from the world’s indifferent gaze. I still feel her elegant frame pressed against my overflowing heart—my senses still falter at the memory of that initial kiss. We walked quietly to find Adrian, whose approach we heard nearby. I begged Adrian to return after escorting his sister home. That same night, as we strolled along the moonlit forest trails, I revealed my entire heart, its joy and its expectations, to my companion. For an instant, he appeared troubled. I should have anticipated this, he remarked, what conflict will follow now!"
}

