parts.text:
{
  "request_id": "5a5b92493f2d67fe31e07977",
  "rewritten_text": "I will submit to you. I see in your face that you know I have no other choice. I know you are honest. The old man kissed her, hurried her into his room, and locked the door. He then rushed back to the Doctor, opened the window and the blind, and placed a hand on the Doctor’s arm to look out into the courtyard together. They looked out at a crowd of about forty or fifty people. The guards had let them in, and they had rushed to use the grindstone, which had been set up in that secluded spot for their use. The workers and their work were terrifying. Two men turned the double-handled grindstone frantically. Their faces, revealed as their long hair whipped back, were more cruel and horrible than the wildest savages. They wore fake eyebrows and mustaches, and their faces were covered in blood and sweat, twisted by howling and wild, sleep-deprived excitement. As they turned the stone, women held wine to their mouths. Between the dripping blood, the spilled wine, and the sparks flying from the stone, the air seemed filled with gore and fire. Every person in the group was smeared with blood. Men stripped to the waist, men in rags, and men wearing stolen lace and silk ribbons all shoved each other to reach the stone, their bodies and clothes stained deep red. Hatchets, knives, bayonets, and swords were all covered in blood. Some hacked swords were tied to the owners' wrists with bloody strips of cloth. As these frantic people grabbed their sharpened weapons and tore into the streets, their eyes burned with the same red frenzy—eyes that any decent person would have given twenty years of their life to stop forever."
}

