  "rewritten_text": "“However,” I replied, handing back the paper, “I remain entirely confused. Even if the treasures of Golconda were the reward for solving this puzzle, I am certain I could never claim them.” “Yet,” Legrand countered, “the answer is far less complex than a quick glance might suggest. These symbols clearly constitute a cipher, yet knowing Kidd, I doubted he could devise anything truly intricate. I concluded it was a basic type, meant to seem impossible to a simple sailor without the proper key.” “You actually deciphered it?” “Easily; I have cracked far more difficult ones. My inclinations have drawn me to such puzzles, and I doubt any human can create a riddle that human intellect cannot eventually unravel. Once I had clear, connected characters, the meaning was simple to extract. In any secret writing, the primary issue is the language, as the method of solution relies on the specific idiom. Usually, one must test various languages based on probability until the correct one appears. Here, the signature provided the answer. The pun on ‘Kidd’ only functions in English. Otherwise, I would have tested Spanish or French, as a pirate in the Spanish Main would likely use those. Instead, I proceeded assuming it was English. You will notice the lack of word breaks. Had they existed, the work would be simpler; I would have analyzed the short words, and a single-letter word like ‘a’ or ‘I’ would have guaranteed success. Without divisions, I began by identifying the most and least frequent characters."
}

