parts.text:
{
  "request_id": "ded4e652942d72e8e2a45b98",
  "rewritten_text": "He abandoned the effort entirely. The boys remained motionless, tracking the agonizingly slow passage of time until the sun finally began to dip below the horizon. One snore stopped abruptly. Injun Joe rose, surveyed the room, and gave his companion a sharp nudge with his boot. He chided the man for his lapse in vigilance, though he conceded that nothing had occurred. The comrade expressed surprise at having dozed off. Joe suggested it was nearly time to depart and inquired about their remaining loot. They decided to leave the six hundred and fifty dollars in silver hidden there until they headed south, though Joe insisted they bury it deeper to ensure its safety. The comrade retrieved the jingling bag from beneath a hearthstone, distributed some cash to both of them, and handed the rest to Joe, who began excavating a corner with his knife. The hidden boys watched with intense fascination, thrilled by the prospect of such a fortune. Suddenly, Joe’s blade hit an obstruction. He discovered a box buried in the dirt and pried it open. Reaching inside, he pulled out a handful of gold coins. The boys above were just as ecstatic as the men below. Joe’s partner suggested they retrieve a rusty pick from the weeds near the fireplace to finish the job quickly."
}

