parts.text:
{
  "request_id": "18a2cfeb988909e5612cd222",
  "rewritten_text": "Recent reports from Rotterdam suggest the city is in a state of intense intellectual agitation. Events have occurred there so unexpected and contrary to established beliefs that I am certain all of Europe is now in an uproar, with the fields of physics and astronomy thrown into total confusion. It seems that on a recent day, a large crowd gathered in the Exchange square of Rotterdam. The weather was unusually warm with little wind, and the people were in good spirits despite occasional light showers falling from scattered white clouds. Around noon, however, a sudden stir moved through the assembly. A roar of conversation erupted, and instantly, ten thousand faces turned toward the sky. Ten thousand pipes were removed from mouths, and a shout like the roar of Niagara Falls echoed throughout the city. The cause of this commotion soon became clear. Emerging from behind a large cloud into the clear blue sky was a strange, solid object. Its shape was so odd and whimsical that the sturdy citizens below could neither understand nor stop staring at it. What could it be? What did it mean? No one knew, and even the mayor, Mynheer Superbus Von Underduk, had no explanation. Lacking any better option, everyone carefully replaced their pipes, tilted their heads to study the object, and paced about, grunting in confusion. Meanwhile, the object drifted lower toward the city, generating even more smoke from the crowd. Within minutes, it was close enough to be clearly identified. It was a balloon, but certainly nothing like any balloon ever seen in Rotterdam before."
}

