parts.text:
{
  "request_id": "b4a1b09ca5d06134aec0a681",
  "rewritten_text": "Well, you rascal, the old lady exclaimed as he entered, why have you stayed away so long? My dear Lady Clem, I am never free, Lord Arthur replied with a smile. I suppose you mean you spend your days with Miss Sybil Merton, shopping and flirting? I cannot fathom why people make such a spectacle of marriage. In my time, we never acted so affectionate in public or private. I assure you I have not seen Sybil in twenty-four hours, Lady Clem. As far as I can tell, she is entirely occupied by her dressmakers. Naturally; that is the only reason you visit an ugly old woman like me. I am surprised you men do not take warning. People once did foolish things for me, and now I am just a rheumatic creature with a wig and a foul temper. If not for dear Lady Jansen, who sends me the most scandalous French novels, I could not endure the day. Doctors are useless, except for collecting fees; they cannot even cure my heartburn. I have brought you a remedy for that, Lady Clem, Lord Arthur said seriously. It is a remarkable invention from America. I do not think I like American inventions, Arthur. I am certain I do not. I read some American novels recently, and they were utter nonsense. Oh, but there is no nonsense in this, Lady Clem! It is a perfect cure. You must promise to try it. Lord Arthur pulled a small box from his pocket and handed it to her. The box is charming, Arthur. Is it truly a gift? That is very sweet. And is this the wonderful medicine? It looks like a candy. I will take it immediately. Good heavens, Lady Clem! Lord Arthur cried, grabbing her hand, you must not do that. It is a homeopathic medicine, and if you take it without having heartburn, it could cause you great harm. Wait until you have an attack, then take it. You will be amazed by the result. I would like to take it now, Lady Clementina said, holding the transparent capsule with its floating bubble of liquid aconitine up to the light. I am sure it is delicious. The truth is, although I despise doctors, I love medicine. However, I will save it for my next attack. And when will that be? Lord Arthur asked eagerly."
}

