  "request_id": "961de04087b645822bd30fc4",
  "rewritten_text": "There was plenty of cold water to finish their meal. Soon, Becky suggested they move on. Tom hesitated, then asked if she could handle some bad news. Becky turned pale but nodded. Tom explained that they had to stay near the water because their last candle was nearly gone. Becky broke down in tears, and despite Tom’s attempts to comfort her, she remained inconsolable. She eventually asked if people would come looking for them. Tom agreed they certainly would, hoping the search had already begun. When Becky asked when they would be missed, Tom suggested it would be when the group returned to the boat. He then realized his mistake, mentioning that her mother would notice her absence as soon as she got home. Becky’s terrified expression confirmed she was not supposed to be home that night, and they both realized it might be Sunday morning before anyone noticed she was missing. They watched the candle burn down until the flame flickered and died, leaving them in total darkness. After an unknown amount of time, they drifted into a deep sleep, only to wake to their ongoing misery. Tom guessed it could be Sunday or Monday. He tried to talk to Becky, but she was too overwhelmed to respond. Tom attempted to shout for help, but the terrifying echoes in the dark silenced him. As time passed, hunger returned. They shared the last of their cake, but it only left them feeling hungrier than before."
}

