parts.text:
{
  "request_id": "aeda5423a8c97f6770c20084",
  "rewritten_text": "I visited several shops to buy the clothes needed for his transformation. Once finished, I headed to Little Britain. Mr. Jaggers was at his desk, but he stood up as soon as I entered and moved to the fireplace. \"Now, Pip,\" he warned, \"be careful.\" \"I will, sir,\" I replied, having prepared my words. \"Don't compromise yourself or anyone else,\" he said. \"Don't tell me anything. I have no curiosity.\" I realized he already knew the man had arrived. \"I only want to confirm what I have been told is true,\" I explained. Mr. Jaggers nodded. \"Did you say 'told' or 'informed'?\" he asked, staring at the floor. \"'Told' implies a conversation, and you cannot speak to a man in New South Wales.\" \"I will say 'informed,' Mr. Jaggers.\" \"Good.\" \"I have been informed by Abel Magwitch that he is my long-term benefactor.\" \"That is the man,\" Jaggers confirmed. \"And only he?\" I asked. \"Only he.\" \"I know you are not responsible for my mistakes, but I always assumed it was Miss Havisham.\" \"As you say, Pip,\" Jaggers replied coolly, biting his finger. \"I am not responsible for that.\" \"It certainly looked like it, sir,\" I said sadly. \"There was no evidence, Pip,\" he replied, shaking his head. \"Never judge by appearances; rely only on evidence. That is the best rule.\" I sighed, standing in silence for a moment. \"I have verified the information, and that is all.\" \"Since Magwitch has revealed himself,\" Jaggers continued, \"you understand how strictly I have always stuck to the facts. You are aware of that?\" \"Quite, sir.\" \"I warned Magwitch when he first wrote to me from New South Wales that he must never expect me to stray from the truth.\""
}

