            "text": "{\n  \"request_id\": \"29c54710206f56bc2e5404d5\",\n  \"rewritten_text\": \"But no, there was something even more spectacular. He would be a pirate! That was it! Now his future was clear and shining with incredible brilliance. How his name would echo across the world and make people tremble! How gloriously he would sail the lively seas in his long, low, black-hulled ship, the Spirit of the Storm, with his grim flag flying high! At the height of his fame, he would return to the old village and march into church, tanned and weathered, wearing a black velvet suit, tall boots, a crimson sash, a belt full of pistols, a scarred cutlass at his side, and a plumed hat, while his skull-and-crossbones flag waved. He imagined the thrill of hearing the whispers, “It’s Tom Sawyer the Pirate—the Black Avenger of the Spanish Main!” Yes, his path was set. He would run away from home to begin his career the very next morning. He started gathering his supplies, digging under a rotten log with his pocketknife until he hit hollow wood. He recited a solemn incantation: “What hasn’t come here, come! What’s here, stay here!” He cleared the dirt to reveal a small wooden box. Inside lay a single marble. Tom was stunned, scratching his head in confusion. “Well, that beats everything!” he muttered, tossing the marble away in frustration. He stood there thinking. His superstition, which he and his friends considered foolproof, had failed. The belief was that if you buried a marble with the right words and waited two weeks, all the marbles you had ever lost would gather there. Since it had failed, his entire worldview was shaken. He had heard of it working many times but never failing. It did not occur to him that he had tried this before and simply forgotten where he buried them. After pondering, he concluded that a witch must have interfered and broken the spell.\"\n}",
