parts.text:
{
  "request_id": "fefb1335fb743c7ff7a1e0d8",
  "rewritten_text": "Reviewing my terrible list of sins, I struggle to believe I am the same being who once cherished noble visions of goodness. Yet it is true; the fallen angel turns into a malicious devil. Even that enemy of God and man had companions in his isolation; I am entirely alone. You, who call Frankenstein a friend, seem to know of my crimes and his suffering. However, his account could not capture the months of misery I endured, trapped in helpless rage. While I destroyed his hopes, I never satisfied my own cravings. I constantly sought love and companionship, only to be rejected. Was there no injustice in that? Am I the only criminal, when all humanity sinned against me? Why do you not hate Felix, who drove me away with insults? Why not despise the villager who tried to kill the one who saved his child? No, they are considered virtuous, while I, the abandoned wretch, am a monster to be kicked and trampled. My blood still boils at the memory of this unfairness. It is true that I am a monster. I have murdered the lovely and the helpless; I have strangled the innocent in their sleep and killed a man who never harmed anyone. I have condemned my creator, the finest of men, to misery, pursuing him to his final ruin. He lies there, cold and dead. You hate me, but your disgust cannot match my own self-loathing. I look at the hands that committed these deeds and the heart that conceived them, longing for the moment when they will haunt me no more. Do not fear further harm from me. My work is nearly finished. No more deaths are required to complete my existence; only my own. I will not hesitate to make this sacrifice. I will leave your ship on the ice raft that brought me here and head to the northernmost point of the globe. I will build my funeral pyre and burn this miserable body to ashes, ensuring that no curious, wicked person can ever study my remains to create another like me."
}

