parts.text:
{
  "request_id": "30d51929c0abe20a82786f3b",
  "rewritten_text": "But no, there was something even more exciting. He would be a pirate! That was it! Now his future seemed clear and brilliant. How his name would spread across the world and make people tremble! He imagined himself sailing the seas in a sleek, black ship called the Spirit of the Storm, his terrifying flag flying high. At the height of his fame, he would return to his old village and walk into church, tanned and rugged, wearing a black velvet outfit, a red sash, and a belt full of pistols and a sword. With his feathered hat and his skull-and-crossbones flag, he would listen with delight as people whispered, \"It’s Tom Sawyer the Pirate—the Black Avenger of the Spanish Main!\" Yes, his career was decided. He would run away from home the very next morning to begin his new life. He started preparing by gathering his supplies. He went to a nearby rotten log and dug under it with his pocketknife until he hit something hollow. He placed his hand there and recited a spell: \"What hasn’t come here, come! What’s here, stay here!\" He cleared away the dirt to reveal a small wooden box. He opened it, expecting a fortune, but found only a single marble. Tom was shocked. He scratched his head, confused, and muttered, \"Well, that beats everything!\" He tossed the marble away and stood thinking. He and his friends had always believed that if you buried a marble with the right spell and left it for two weeks, all the marbles you had ever lost would gather there. The fact that it had failed shook his entire belief system. He had heard of it working many times but never failing. It didn't occur to him that he had tried this before and simply forgotten where he buried them. After thinking it over, he decided that a witch must have interfered and broken the charm."
}

