  "rewritten_text": "Do you intend to play? The spy turned toward Mr. Lorry with a servile air, suggesting that a man of his age and kindness might convince his younger companion that playing the mentioned Ace was beneath his station. He acknowledged his own disreputable role as a spy, yet questioned why a gentleman would stoop to such behavior. Carton checked his watch and replied that he would play his Ace without hesitation in a few moments. When the spy attempted to invoke respect for his sister, Carton countered that he could show no greater respect for her than by removing her brother from her life. The spy faltered, unable to penetrate Carton’s inscrutable demeanor. Carton then mused aloud about another card, asking after the associate who claimed to frequent the prisons. The spy quickly dismissed the man as a Frenchman of no importance. Carton repeated the words mechanically, claiming to recognize the face. Despite the spy’s denials, Carton suddenly realized the man was Cly, whom they had previously encountered at the Old Bailey. Barsad smiled, his nose tilting, and remarked that Carton was being hasty and granting him an advantage."
}

