parts.text:
{
  "request_id": "d89a9ce0711b233a31b688ee",
  "rewritten_text": "If I cannot live on that, I will not ask for help. Is that satisfactory? A massive roar of applause followed, and the king’s voice rose above it, ordering his guards to release me. He declared that I was now his right hand, granted great power, and should be honored by everyone. He commanded that the darkness be lifted so the world could rejoice. I replied that while my own shame mattered little, it would dishonor the king if his minister remained naked. I asked for my clothes to be returned. The king insisted I be dressed like a prince instead. My plan was to delay until the eclipse was total, as I could not actually end the darkness. Requesting new clothes bought some time, but not enough, so I claimed the king might regret his impulsive decision. I insisted on waiting to see if he remained firm in his choice. Though no one was happy, I held my ground. As the sky grew pitch black, the crowd groaned in terror at the cold breeze and the appearance of stars. I was relieved when the eclipse finally became total, though everyone else was miserable. I announced that the king had kept his word, then raised my hands and solemnly commanded the enchantment to end. Silence filled the darkness for a moment. When the sun finally reappeared, the crowd erupted in cheers and rushed toward me, showering me with gratitude. Clarence was certainly among the first to reach me."
}

