parts.text:
{
  "request_id": "4b34418419c8aa7f78194022",
  "rewritten_text": "This must have been the period of Mr. Elliot’s life that has always made me curious, Anne said. It was around the time he first met my father and sister. I never met him myself, only heard of him, but his behavior toward them and the circumstances of his marriage never seemed to match the man I see today. It suggested a completely different person. I know everything, Mrs. Smith replied. He met your father and sister before I knew him, but he spoke of them constantly. I know he was invited to visit but chose not to go. I can answer questions you might not expect, and I knew all about his marriage at the time. I was the friend he confided in regarding his plans. Although I did not know his wife beforehand due to her lower social status, I knew her for years afterward and can answer anything you wish to ask. No, Anne said, I have no specific questions about her. I always understood they were unhappy. I only want to know why he avoided my father back then, as my father was quite willing to welcome him. Why did he pull away? At that time, Mrs. Smith explained, Mr. Elliot had one goal: to make his fortune quickly, specifically through marriage. He was determined not to ruin his prospects with an unwise match. He believed, rightly or wrongly, that your father and sister were trying to set him up with your sister, and he knew that would not provide the wealth and independence he wanted. That was his reason for avoiding them. He told me the whole story; he hid nothing from me. It is strange that after leaving you in Bath, the first person I became close to after my marriage was your cousin, and through him, I constantly heard about your father and sister."
}

