parts.text:
{
  "request_id": "d8e33bc259af3baf7142a4fb",
  "rewritten_text": "Stop the starboard! Stop the larboard! Move ahead on the starboard! Stop her! Let the outside wheel turn slowly! Get that headline out! Quickly now! Get the spring-line out—what are you doing? Wrap it around that stump! Get the gangplank ready—let it go! Engines off! Tom kept whitewashing, ignoring the steamboat. Ben stared for a moment and said, \"Hey! You are stuck, aren't you?\" Tom did not answer. He studied his last stroke like an artist, brushed again, and checked the result. Ben walked up beside him. Tom wanted the apple, but he kept working. Ben said, \"Hello, friend, you have to work, huh?\" Tom turned suddenly. \"Oh, it is you, Ben! I did not notice you.\" \"I am going swimming. Don't you wish you could? But you would rather work, right? Of course you would!\" Tom looked at him and asked, \"What do you call work?\" \"Well, isn't that work?\" Tom went back to painting, answering casually, \"Maybe it is, maybe it isn't. All I know is that it suits Tom Sawyer.\" \"Come on, you don't mean to say you like it?\" The brush kept moving. \"Like it? I don't see why I shouldn't. Does a boy get a chance to whitewash a fence every day?\" That changed things. Ben stopped eating his apple. Tom brushed carefully, stepped back to check the effect, and added a few touches. Ben watched every move, becoming increasingly interested. Finally, he said, \"Tom, let me whitewash a little.\" Tom thought about it, then shook his head. \"No, I don't think that would work, Ben. Aunt Polly is very particular about this fence because it faces the street. If it were the back fence, I wouldn't mind, and neither would she. She is very strict; it has to be done perfectly. I don't think one boy in two thousand can do it right.\" \"Is that so? Come on, let me try. Just a little. I would let you do it if I were you.\" \"Ben, I would like to, honestly. But Aunt Polly—well, Jim wanted to do it, but she wouldn't let him. Sid wanted to do it, and she wouldn't let him either.\""
}

