parts.text:
{
  "request_id": "fd30537a580278781c2bed14",
  "rewritten_text": "The narrow alleys eventually opened into a wide, vacant area filled with animal pens and signs of a livestock market. Sikes slowed down, as the girl could no longer keep up with their frantic pace. He turned to Oliver and gruffly ordered him to take Nancy’s hand. When Oliver hesitated and glanced around, Sikes growled, \"Do you hear me?\" They stood in a dark corner, far from any passersby. Realizing resistance was useless, Oliver held out his hand, which Nancy gripped tightly. Sikes grabbed Oliver’s other hand and called, \"Here, Bull’s-Eye!\" The dog looked up and growled. Sikes pressed his hand against Oliver’s throat and warned, \"Listen, boy! If he says a single word, grab him! Understand?\" The dog growled again, licking his lips and staring at Oliver as if eager to tear out his throat. \"He’s as ready as any person, I swear,\" Sikes said, looking at the dog with grim approval. \"Now you know what to expect, so go ahead and shout if you want; the dog will put a stop to that quickly. Move on, kid!\" Bull’s-Eye wagged his tail at the praise, let out one more warning growl at Oliver, and led the way. They were crossing Smithfield, though it could have been anywhere for all Oliver knew. The night was dark and foggy. Shop lights barely pierced the thick mist, which shrouded the streets in gloom and made the unfamiliar surroundings feel even more unsettling. They had walked only a short distance when a deep church bell began to toll. At the first sound, both his captors stopped and looked toward the noise. \"It’s eight o’clock, Bill,\" Nancy said when the bell stopped. \"What’s the point of telling me? I can hear it, can’t I?\" Sikes replied. \"I wonder if they can hear it,\" Nancy mused. \"Of course they can,\" Sikes answered. \"It was fair time when I was arrested, and I could hear every penny trumpet squeaking. Once I was locked up for the night, the noise outside made the jail feel so silent that I could have smashed my head against the iron door.\""
}

