  "request_id": "a37c28571eee724d43cddd9c",
  "rewritten_text": "One final word, Rose. Dearest Rose, just one! Harry pleaded, blocking her path. If my circumstances had been less fortunate—if a quiet, obscure life had been my lot, or if I were poor, ill, or weak—would you have rejected me? Or does my potential for wealth and status inspire this hesitation? Please do not force me to answer, Rose replied. The situation is hypothetical and will never occur; it is unfair to press me. If your answer matches my hopes, Harry insisted, it would brighten my solitary journey. It is no small thing to offer such comfort to one who loves you above all. In the name of my deep devotion and all I have endured for you, answer me. If your life had been different, Rose conceded, if you were only slightly above my station, and I could have been a source of comfort in a humble life rather than a hindrance in high society, I would have been spared this pain. I am happy now, but I admit I would have been happier then. Memories of girlhood dreams flooded her mind, bringing tears that offered a strange relief. I cannot help this vulnerability, but it strengthens my resolve, Rose said, offering her hand. I must go. I ask for one promise, Harry said. Within a year, I may speak to you on this matter one final time. Not to pressure me into changing my mind, for that would be futile, Rose replied with a sad smile. No, Harry said, only to hear you confirm your decision. I will offer you whatever status I have attained, and if you still refuse, I will never again attempt to sway you. Then let it be so, Rose agreed. It is merely one more moment of pain, and by then, I may be better prepared to endure it. She reached out her hand once more."
}

