parts.text:
{
  "request_id": "bf9fc99cacb956ce98d09e9d",
  "rewritten_text": "I walked quickly, reaching my college soon. I shivered, suddenly realizing the creature I left in my apartment might still be there. I dreaded seeing the monster, but feared even more that Henry might encounter him. Asking him to wait at the stairs, I rushed to my room. My hand was on the lock before I paused, trembling. I threw the door open, expecting a ghost, but the room was empty. Relieved, I ran back to Clerval. We went upstairs, but I could not contain my agitation. My pulse raced, and I paced frantically, laughing loudly. Clerval initially thought I was just happy to see him, but my wild eyes and hysterical laughter soon alarmed him. Victor, what is wrong? he asked. You look ill. Do not ask, I cried, shielding my eyes as I imagined the monster entering. Save me! I felt the creature grab me, struggled, and collapsed. Poor Clerval; our reunion had turned into a nightmare. I remained unconscious, unaware of his distress. This began a nervous fever that lasted months. Henry nursed me alone, shielding my father and Elizabeth from the truth of my condition."
}

