parts.text:
{
  "request_id": "3b3ee0d5cd328033c0a118e3",
  "rewritten_text": "It is just a tick. Where did you find it? In the forest. What will you trade for it? I am not sure, as I do not care to sell. Very well, it is a tiny tick regardless. Anyone can catch a tick that is not their own, but I am content. It is sufficient for me. Nonsense, there are ticks everywhere. I could gather a thousand if I chose. Then why do you not? Because you know you cannot. This is an early specimen, I believe. It is the first I have spotted this season. Listen, Huck, I will trade you my tooth for it. Let me see it. Tom unwrapped a piece of paper, and Huckleberry examined it with longing. The urge was powerful. Finally, he asked if it was authentic. Tom pulled back his lip to reveal the gap. Very well, it is a deal. Tom placed the tick inside the percussion-cap box that had recently held the pinchbug, and the boys parted, both feeling richer. Upon arriving at the small, detached schoolhouse, Tom marched inside with the air of someone who had hurried. He hung his hat and sat down with purposeful speed. The teacher, perched in his large chair, was napping to the sound of the students studying. The noise woke him. Thomas Sawyer! Tom knew that his full name meant impending trouble. Sir! Come here. Why are you late again? Tom prepared to lie, but then he noticed two yellow braids hanging down a back he recognized with a jolt of affection. Beside that figure was the only empty seat on the girls' side. He immediately replied that he had stopped to speak with Huckleberry Finn. The master froze in disbelief. The room went silent as the students wondered if Tom had lost his senses. The teacher asked him to repeat himself, and Tom did so clearly. Thomas Sawyer, this is a shocking admission. A simple punishment will not suffice. Remove your jacket. The master struck him until his arm grew weary and the switches were nearly gone. Then he ordered Tom to sit with the girls as a warning. The laughter that spread through the room seemed to embarrass the boy, but in truth, he was overwhelmed by his adoration for his idol and the thrilling fortune of his new seat."
}

