parts.text:
{
  "request_id": "5525b360aedca14dcda4c2cf",
  "rewritten_text": "Listen to me; I have mastered the language of despair. I am despair itself, a strange, triumphant force. Yet that is a lie, for the dark wave is not bitter. We simply close our eyes in a gentle sleep, and upon waking, we are free. Do not delay, you slow one! Look at this inviting potion. I am a spirit of mercy, not a mere woman, urging you to drink. As I spoke, I watched his face. His exquisite beauty and the heavenly compassion in his eyes, filled with earnest wonder, shattered my resolve. My stern despair dissolved into soft grief. His own eyes grew moist as he took my hands and sat beside me. This is a tragic path you propose, my dear friend, and your suffering must be profound to drive you to such thoughts. You crave death, yet you fear it and want me to join you. I lack your courage; I dare not die, even with you. Listen to me before you try to convince me, even if your desperate eloquence could make death seem more inviting than heaven. I have harbored such dark thoughts myself and longed for the end, but I have overcome that phantom. Just as you played the role of Despair, I will be your guide to lead you safely from this cavern. Listen and let your heart soften. We do not understand this world’s strange mix of good and evil, yet we are placed here to live and hope. I do not know what we should hope for, but there is some greater good we must seek; that is our purpose. If misfortune strikes, we must fight it and continue our search. Whether this hope prepares us for another life or simply allows us to smooth the path for those who follow, I cannot say."
}

