parts.text:
{
  "request_id": "3b81093132abeb7340ca3af7",
  "rewritten_text": "Tom managed to scratch the cupboard and was planning to work on the bureau when he was summoned to prepare for Sunday school. Mary provided a tin basin and soap, which he placed on a bench outside. He dipped the soap, poured the water onto the ground, and returned to the kitchen to dry his face on the towel. Mary took the towel away, chiding him for his behavior and insisting he use the water. Tom felt flustered but eventually steeled himself to wash properly. He returned to the kitchen with eyes closed, dripping with soap and water. However, his cleaning was incomplete, leaving a mask-like line of dirt around his chin and neck. Mary scrubbed him until he was thoroughly clean, brushing his damp hair into neat curls. Tom later flattened these curls, as he despised them as effeminate. Mary then produced his Sunday best, the only alternative to his everyday attire. She finished dressing him, buttoning his jacket, adjusting his collar, and placing his straw hat on his head. Tom appeared much improved but felt deeply uneasy, as the restriction of clean, formal clothing irritated him. He hoped she would overlook his shoes, but she greased them with tallow as expected. Frustrated, Tom complained that he was constantly forced to do things against his will."
}

