parts.text:
{
  "request_id": "566a7c253b86487beb7bbe49",
  "rewritten_text": "Biddy wept, and the dim garden, the lane, and the emerging stars grew hazy before my own eyes. \"Has nothing ever been found, Biddy?\" \"Nothing.\" \"Do you know what has become of Orlick?\" \"Judging by his dusty clothes, I suspect he labors in the quarries.\" \"You have seen him, then? Why do you stare at that dark tree in the lane?\" \"I saw him there the night she passed away.\" \"That was not the final time, was it, Biddy?\" \"No; I have spotted him there since we began walking here. It is futile,\" Biddy said, touching my arm as I prepared to rush out, \"you know I would not mislead you; he was only there for a moment and has already departed.\" My fury reignited upon learning she was still haunted by that man, and I felt a deep resentment toward him. I expressed my resolve to spend any amount or exert any effort to banish him from the region. Gradually, she guided me toward a calmer conversation, describing how Joe cherished me and never uttered a complaint—she did not explicitly mention me, but I understood—always fulfilling his duties with a steady hand, a reserved tongue, and a kind heart. \"Truly, one could hardly praise him enough,\" I remarked. \"And Biddy, we must discuss these matters frequently, as I intend to visit here often now. I will not abandon poor Joe.\" Biddy remained silent. \"Biddy, do you not hear me?\" \"Yes, Mr. Pip.\" \"Aside from your calling me Mr. Pip—which strikes me as poor taste—what do you mean?\" \"What do I mean?\" Biddy asked timidly. \"Biddy,\" I said with self-righteous insistence, \"I must ask what you mean by this?\" \"By this?\" Biddy repeated. \"Do not echo me,\" I snapped. \"You never used to echo, Biddy.\" \"Used not!\" Biddy exclaimed. \"Oh, Mr. Pip! Used!\" I decided to drop that subject. After another quiet stroll through the garden, I returned to my primary point. \"Biddy, I mentioned that I would visit Joe often, a statement you met with pointed silence. Please, tell me why.\" \"Are you truly certain that you will visit him often?\" Biddy asked, pausing on the narrow path to look at me under the starlight with clear, honest eyes."
}

