parts.text:
{
  "request_id": "440c16eeec50f381d457ddb5",
  "rewritten_text": "Suddenly, Mr. Podgers dropped Lord Arthur’s right hand and grabbed his left, leaning down so far to inspect it that his glasses nearly touched the palm. For a second, his face turned pale with horror, but he quickly regained his composure. Looking up at Lady Windermere, he forced a smile and said, It is the hand of a charming young man. Of course it is, Lady Windermere replied, but will he be a charming husband? That is what I want to know. All charming young men are, Mr. Podgers said. I do not think a husband should be too fascinating, Lady Jedburgh murmured thoughtfully, it is dangerous. My dear, they are never too fascinating, Lady Windermere cried. But I want details. Details are the only things that matter. What will happen to Lord Arthur? Well, within the next few months, Lord Arthur will go on a voyage. Oh, his honeymoon, of course! And he will lose a relative. Not his sister, I hope? Lady Jedburgh asked sadly. Certainly not his sister, Mr. Podgers answered with a wave of his hand, just a distant relative. Well, I am disappointed, Lady Windermere said. I have nothing to tell Sybil tomorrow. No one cares about distant relatives anymore. Still, she should probably have a black silk dress ready; it is always useful for church. Now, let us go to supper. They have likely eaten everything, but we might find some hot soup. François used to make excellent soup, but he is so distracted by politics lately that I am never sure about him. I wish General Boulanger would stay quiet. Duchess, you must be tired? Not at all, dear Gladys, the Duchess replied, waddling toward the door. I have enjoyed myself, and the palm reader is fascinating. Flora, where is my fan? Oh, thank you, Sir Thomas. And my lace shawl? Thank you, Sir Thomas, you are very kind. The woman finally made it downstairs, dropping her perfume bottle only twice. Throughout this, Lord Arthur Savile stood by the fireplace, feeling a sense of dread and impending doom. He smiled sadly at his sister as she walked past on Lord Plymdale’s arm, looking beautiful in pink silk and pearls. He barely heard Lady Windermere calling him to follow. He thought of Sybil Merton, and the fear that anything could separate them brought tears to his eyes."
}

