parts.text:
{
  "request_id": "f3ccf93239ad424ca1f4acbe",
  "rewritten_text": "He mounted the spirited horse that had carried him to victory in Greece, exhausting himself with intense exercise to drown his mental anguish in physical exertion. He slowly recovered, finally emerging from the haze of fever and passion like one recovering from poison, ready for calm reflection. He considered his next steps, struck by how long he had let madness dictate his actions. A month had passed since he last saw Evadne, and her influence over him had faded; he was no longer her slave or her lover. He resolved never to see her again, hoping to earn Perdita’s trust through his complete return. Yet, he could not help but picture the Greek girl’s miserable home, which she had refused to trade for luxury out of principle. He recalled her former splendor in Constantinople and contrasted it with her current poverty, her daily toil, and her gaunt, starving face. Compassion filled him; he decided to visit her one last time to arrange for her restoration to society before ending their connection permanently. He then reflected on how he had avoided Perdita for a month, fleeing from his own guilt. He felt cheerful as he resolved to fix this, planning to erase this lapse with future devotion. He remembered his promise to attend a festival that evening, October 19th, celebrating his election as Protector. He viewed it as a positive omen. He would briefly visit Evadne to explain his long absence, then return to Perdita, his public duties, and his position of power. Following the events described, Perdita had anticipated a total shift in Raymond’s behavior, hoping for open communication and a return to the affectionate intimacy that had once defined their life."
}

