  "rewritten_text": "He acted with extreme stubbornness, repeating only \"that cursed bug\" throughout our journey. I carried two lanterns, while Legrand swung the beetle on a piece of string like a magician. Seeing this clear sign of his mental instability, I nearly cried. I decided to play along for now, hoping to find a better way to help him later. My attempts to ask about our destination failed; he refused to discuss anything else, answering only with \"we shall see!\" We crossed the creek in a small boat and climbed the mainland hills, heading northwest through wild, empty land. Legrand led us confidently, stopping briefly to check landmarks he had set previously. After two hours, as the sun set, we reached a desolate plateau near the top of a steep, wooded hill. The area was filled with large, loose boulders held in place only by the trees, and deep ravines added to the grim atmosphere. The ground was covered in thick brambles that we could only clear with a scythe. Jupiter followed Legrand’s orders to cut a path to a massive tulip tree. It stood among several oaks, towering over them with its majestic shape and wide, beautiful branches."
}

