parts.text:
{
  "request_id": "2f135438c042ecb853fe71ee",
  "rewritten_text": "Knights in heavy armor could not move quickly. Even on firm ground without snow or mud, they would likely maintain a pace of seven miles an hour. After changing horses twice, they should arrive around six o'clock. There would still be enough daylight to spot the white cloth on my arm, allowing me to take command. We would surround the prison and rescue the king immediately. It would be a dramatic scene, though I would have preferred doing it at noon for more theatrical effect. To improve my chances, I decided to find people I recognized and reveal my identity, which might resolve our situation without needing the knights. However, I had to be careful. I needed to acquire fine clothing, but I could not simply put it on all at once. I had to buy increasingly expensive outfits from different shops until I reached silk and velvet. I began my plan, but it failed instantly. Turning a corner, I ran into one of our slaves with a watchman. I coughed, and he looked at me with a piercing gaze, as if he recognized the sound. I ducked into a shop and pretended to browse while watching them. They stopped to talk while looking toward the door. I decided to escape through the back. I told the shopkeeper I was an undercover officer searching for an escaped slave and asked her to tell my partner at the door to move to the end of the alley to intercept the fugitive. Eager to see a notorious criminal, she hurried off to deliver the message."
}

