parts.text:
{
  "request_id": "3a19e3018a75e4235f343899",
  "rewritten_text": "When Tom woke up, he was momentarily confused about his surroundings. He sat up, rubbed his eyes, and realized he was in the woods. It was a cool, gray dawn, and the forest felt peaceful and still. Not a leaf moved, and the silence was absolute. Dewdrops clung to the grass, and a thin trail of smoke rose from the campfire where Joe and Huck were still asleep. Soon, birds began to call, and a woodpecker started hammering. As the morning light brightened, the forest came to life. Tom watched in wonder as nature woke up. A small green worm crawled across a leaf, measuring the distance as it moved. When it finally climbed onto Tom’s leg, he was delighted, taking it as a sign that he would soon have a new suit of clothes—a pirate uniform. Nearby, a line of ants worked busily, one struggling to carry a dead spider up a tree. Tom recited a rhyme to a ladybug, and when it flew away, he felt satisfied, knowing he had tricked it as he often did. He poked a tumblebug, watching it curl up and play dead. By now, the birds were loud and active. A catbird sang from a branch above, mimicking other birds, while a bright blue jay landed nearby to inspect the boys with curiosity. A gray squirrel and a fox squirrel scurried past, pausing to chatter at the intruders, as these wild animals had likely never seen humans before and were unsure whether to be afraid."
}

