parts.text:
{
  "request_id": "b6fb36f6aff980d21095ea9d",
  "rewritten_text": "I went from shop to shop, buying what was needed to change his appearance. Once finished, I headed to Little Britain. Mr. Jaggers was at his desk, but stood up as I entered, moving to stand before his fireplace. \"Now, Pip,\" he warned, \"be careful.\" \"I will, sir,\" I replied, having prepared my words. \"Don't commit yourself,\" Jaggers said, \"and don't commit anyone else. You understand—anyone. Don't tell me anything; I don't want to know, and I am not curious.\" It was clear he knew the man had arrived. \"I only want to confirm what I have been told is true,\" I said. \"I have no hope it is false, but I must verify it.\" Jaggers nodded. \"Did you say 'told' or 'informed'?\" he asked, tilting his head to listen to the floor. \"'Told' implies verbal communication, and you cannot speak to a man in New South Wales.\" \"I will say 'informed,' Mr. Jaggers.\" \"Good.\" \"I have been informed by Abel Magwitch that he is my long-unknown benefactor.\" \"That is the man,\" Jaggers confirmed, \"in New South Wales.\" \"And only him?\" I asked. \"Only him.\" \"I am not unreasonable enough to hold you responsible for my mistakes, but I always assumed it was Miss Havisham.\" \"As you say, Pip,\" Jaggers replied, eyeing me coolly while biting his finger, \"I am not responsible for that.\" \"And yet it seemed so likely,\" I pleaded, feeling discouraged. \"Not a shred of evidence, Pip,\" Jaggers said, shaking his head. \"Never judge by appearances; judge by evidence. There is no better rule.\" \"I have nothing more to say,\" I sighed after a silence. \"I have verified the information, and that is the end of it.\" \"And now that Magwitch has revealed himself,\" Jaggers continued, \"you understand how strictly I have always adhered to the facts in our dealings. There has never been the slightest deviation. You are aware of that?\" \"Quite, sir.\" \"I warned Magwitch when he first wrote to me from New South Wales that he must never expect me to deviate from the strict truth.\""
}

