parts.text:
{
  "request_id": "979a3dff6a1ba541baf5fe0c",
  "rewritten_text": "I will submit to you. I see in your expression that you know I have no other choice. I trust you. The old man kissed her, hurried her into his room, and locked the door. He then rushed back to the Doctor, opened the window and partially raised the blind, and placed a hand on the Doctor’s arm as they looked into the courtyard. They saw a crowd of forty or fifty people. The house’s occupants had admitted them, and they had rushed in to use the grindstone, which had been set up in that secluded spot. The workers and their work were terrifying. Two men turned the double-handled grindstone with frantic intensity. Their faces, revealed as their long hair whipped back, were more cruel than those of the most savage barbarians. Wearing fake eyebrows and mustaches, their hideous features were slick with blood and sweat, twisted by howling, and wild with sleep-deprived excitement. As they turned the stone, women held wine to their mouths. Between the dripping blood, the spilled wine, and the sparks flying from the stone, the air seemed filled with gore and fire. Every person in the group was stained with blood. Men stripped to the waist, men in rags, and men adorned with stolen lace and silk ribbons all shoved each other to reach the stone, their bodies and clothing soaked in red. Hatchets, knives, bayonets, and swords were all being sharpened, each coated in blood. Some hacked blades were tied to their owners' wrists with strips of linen or fabric, all stained the same deep color. As these frantic individuals snatched their weapons from the sparks and tore into the streets, that same red hue burned in their frenzied eyes—eyes that any decent person would have given twenty years of their life to stop forever."
}

