parts.text:
{
  "request_id": "fbbab90e5f393b100d0894c3",
  "rewritten_text": "Shortly after midday, the boys took a small boat belonging to an absent neighbor and set off. Once they were several miles past Cave Hollow, Tom spoke up. \"Notice how this bluff looks identical all the way from the hollow—no dwellings, no wood-yards, just uniform brush. But see that white patch where the earth slid away? That is one of my markers. We will go ashore here.\" They disembarked. \"Now, Huck, you could reach the hole I escaped from with a fishing pole from where we stand. Try to locate it.\" Huck searched the area thoroughly but found nothing. Tom marched triumphantly into a dense cluster of sumac bushes and declared, \"Here it is! Look, Huck; it is the most hidden spot in the region. Keep this to yourself. I have long wanted to be a robber, but finding a place like this was the challenge. We have it now, and we will keep it secret, though we shall include Joe Harper and Ben Rogers—a gang is essential for any real prestige. Tom Sawyer’s Gang—it sounds magnificent, doesn't it, Huck?\" \"It certainly does, Tom. And who are we going to rob?\" \"Oh, just about anyone. We will waylay travelers—that is the usual method.\" \"And kill them?\" \"Not always. We will hold them in the cave until they pay a ransom.\" \"What is a ransom?\" \"Money. You force them to collect all they can from their friends; if they cannot pay after a year, then you kill them. That is the standard procedure. You never kill the women, though. You lock them up, but you do not harm them. They are always beautiful, wealthy, and terrified. You take their jewelry, but you always remove your hat and speak courteously. Robbers are the most polite people—you will see that in any book. Eventually, the women grow to love you, and after a week or two in the cave, they stop weeping and refuse to leave. If you tried to drive them out, they would return. That is how it happens in all the stories.\" \"Why, that is truly excellent, Tom. I think it is even better than being a pirate.\" \"Yes, it has advantages, since it is near home and the circus and such.\" With preparations complete, the boys entered the opening, Tom leading the way. They struggled to the far end of the tunnel, secured their knotted kite strings, and pressed onward."
}

