  "rewritten_text": "He kept one secret from his dear friends, a private devotion nurtured since childhood that he dared not share, fearing they might mock the intensity of a passion he considered his very lifeblood. Near his family estate lived a man of modest means with three lovely daughters. The eldest, Diana, possessed not only striking beauty but a sharp intellect and a gentle spirit. Having been playmates since infancy, she was a favorite of his mother, and they spent every school vacation together. Influenced by literature that introduced the concept of romance to the impressionable, he began speaking the language of love to her by age eleven. Though two years his senior, Diana was less worldly; she accepted his youthful declarations with innocent ignorance. As she matured and realized the nature of their bond, her heart was already committed, leaving her only to fear his potential inconstancy. Their affection deepened as they grew, becoming an inseparable part of his existence. Despite his dread that peers might judge him for loving someone of lower social standing, he remained steadfast in his resolve to marry her once he could overcome the necessary obstacles. Diana was entirely deserving of his profound devotion."
}

