parts.text:
{
  "request_id": "af12cfe27b062b845900ebbe",
  "rewritten_text": "There was something so striking about the growing intensity in Mr. Wopsle’s gaze, and he seemed so preoccupied and bewildered, that I could not understand it. I pondered it long after he had ascended into the clouds within a large watch-case, and I still could not make sense of it. I was still thinking about it an hour later when I left the theater and found him waiting for me by the door. How are you? I asked, shaking his hand as we walked down the street. I saw that you saw me. Saw you, Mr. Pip? he replied. Yes, of course I saw you. But who else was there? Who else? It is the strangest thing, Mr. Wopsle said, drifting back into his vacant expression, and yet I could swear it was him. Growing alarmed, I begged Mr. Wopsle to explain. Whether I would have noticed him initially if you had not been there, I cannot be certain, he continued in that same distant manner, yet I think I would have. Involuntarily, I looked around, as I usually did when heading home, for his mysterious words gave me a chill. Oh, he cannot be in sight, Mr. Wopsle said. He left before I went off stage. I saw him go. Given my reasons for suspicion, I even doubted this poor actor. I suspected a plot to trick me into an admission. Therefore, I watched him as we walked but said nothing. I had a ridiculous notion that he must be with you, Mr. Pip, until I saw you were completely unaware of him, sitting behind you like a ghost. My earlier chill returned, but I resolved to remain silent, as it was possible he was being used to make me link these references to Provis. Of course, I was certain Provis had not been there. I imagine you are puzzled by me, Mr. Pip; I can see that you are. But it is so strange! You will hardly believe what I am about to tell you. I could hardly believe it myself if you told me. Indeed? I asked. Yes, indeed. Mr. Pip, do you remember that Christmas Day long ago, when you were a child and I dined at Gargery’s, and soldiers came to the door to have handcuffs mended? I remember it very well. And you remember the chase after two convicts, that we joined in, that Gargery carried you on his back, and that I took the lead while you kept up with me as best you could?"
}

