parts.text:
{
  "request_id": "67893626da924a73366868ad",
  "rewritten_text": "Few possessed such a pure heart and genuine humility, combined with a firm belief in her own integrity and the goodness of others. She had lived a quiet life since birth. Although she lost her mother early, her father dedicated himself to her education, following his own unconventional methods. She was well-versed in the heroes of ancient Greece, Rome, and historical England, yet she knew little of current events. She had read few modern authors, but her education was otherwise extensive. While she seemed less experienced in the ways of society than he, her knowledge was deeper and more grounded. Even if her beauty and sweetness had not captivated him, her intellect would have held him spellbound. He looked to her as his guide, finding joy in the sense of inferiority she sometimes inspired in him. When he was nineteen, his mother died. He left college, distanced himself from his old friends, and sought comfort in the company of his beloved Diana. This brief separation gave him the courage to assert his independence. Believing his friends would not dare mock his marriage once it was official, he secured his guardian’s consent with some difficulty and her father’s approval more easily. Without telling anyone else, he married Diana by his twentieth birthday. He loved her passionately, and her tenderness consumed his thoughts. He invited some college friends to visit, but their frivolity disgusted him. Diana had opened his eyes, helping him transition into manhood. He was surprised he had ever adopted the shallow attitudes of his peers or feared their judgment. He abandoned his old friendships not out of fickleness, but because he realized they were truly unworthy of him."
}

