parts.text:
{
  "request_id": "667a4271f2dbdf0cfe40de3d",
  "rewritten_text": "When I review my terrible sins, I struggle to believe I am the same being who once dreamed of the beauty and majesty of goodness. Yet it is true; a fallen angel becomes a cruel devil. Even that enemy of God and man had companions in his misery, but I am entirely alone. You, who call Frankenstein a friend, seem to know of my crimes and his suffering. However, his account could not capture the months of agony I endured while trapped in useless rage. While I destroyed his hopes, I never satisfied my own desires. I constantly craved love and friendship, yet I was always rejected. Was there no injustice in this? Am I the only criminal when all of humanity sinned against me? Why do you not hate Felix, who drove his friend away with insults? Why do you not despise the villager who tried to kill the man who saved his child? Apparently, they are considered virtuous, while I, the abandoned wretch, am a monster to be kicked and trampled. Even now, my blood boils at the memory of this unfairness. It is true that I am a wretch. I have murdered the lovely and the helpless; I have strangled the innocent in their sleep and killed a man who never harmed anyone. I have brought misery to my creator, the finest of men, and pursued him to his ruin. There he lies, cold in death. You hate me, but your disgust cannot match my own self-loathing. I look at the hands that committed these deeds and the heart that imagined them, longing for the moment when I no longer exist. Do not fear that I will cause more harm. My work is nearly finished. I do not need to kill anyone else to complete my existence; I only need to end my own life. I will not hesitate to make this sacrifice. I will leave your ship on the ice raft that brought me here and head to the furthest north. I will build my funeral pyre and burn this miserable body to ashes, so that no curious person can ever study my remains to create another like me."
}

