parts.text:
{
  "request_id": "efc015d43822b3db2674af18",
  "rewritten_text": "I shall submit to you. Your expression confirms you realize I have no other choice. I trust you are sincere. The elderly man kissed her, ushered her into his chamber, and locked the door. He then rushed back to the Doctor, opened the window and partially raised the blind, and, placing a hand on the Doctor’s arm, gazed with him into the courtyard. They looked down upon a crowd of perhaps forty or fifty people. Those occupying the house had admitted them, and they had hurried in to operate the grindstone, which had been positioned there as a secluded and practical location. The workers and their labor were truly terrifying. Two men turned the double-handled grindstone with frantic intensity. As their long hair whipped back, their faces appeared more cruel and grotesque than the most savage warriors. Adorned with fake eyebrows and mustaches, their hideous features were slick with blood and sweat, twisted by howling, and wild with animalistic fervor and exhaustion. As these brutes labored, women offered them wine; between the dripping blood, the spilled wine, and the sparks flying from the stone, the air seemed filled with gore and flame. Every person in the group was stained with blood. Men stripped to the waist, others in tattered clothing, and some wearing stolen lace and silk ribbons—all were covered in the same crimson mark as they jostled to reach the sharpening stone. Hatchets, knives, bayonets, and swords were all coated in red. Some damaged blades were bound to the owners' wrists with blood-soaked rags. As these frenzied individuals snatched their sharpened weapons and rushed into the streets, their eyes burned with the same murderous intensity—a gaze that any civilized observer would have gladly ended with a single shot."
}

