parts.text:
{
  "request_id": "fd51fd11cd46b67bc4f9866a",
  "rewritten_text": "The little man possessed a disproportionately broad frame, giving his figure a comical roundness. His feet were hidden, though a suspicious, horny substance occasionally poked through a tear in the bottom of his hat. His hands were massive, his hair gray and tied in a queue. His nose was long, crooked, and inflamed; his eyes were sharp and brilliant; his cheeks and chin were wrinkled, puffy, and double. Remarkably, he had no visible ears. He wore a loose sky-blue satin coat with matching breeches buckled at the knees, a bright yellow vest, and a white taffeta cap worn jauntily. A large, blood-red silk handkerchief was tied in a flamboyant bow around his throat. Upon descending to about one hundred feet above the ground, the man grew suddenly anxious and reluctant to land. He struggled to toss sand from a canvas bag, causing his craft to hover. Agitated, he pulled a heavy leather pocketbook from his coat, examined it with surprise, and removed a large letter sealed with red wax and tied with tape. He dropped it at the feet of the burgomaster, Superbus Von Underduk. As the official bent to retrieve it, the aeronaut, eager to leave, dumped six full bags of ballast to gain altitude. They struck the burgomaster, rolling him over twenty-one times before the entire city. Naturally, Underduk would not let such an insult go unpunished."
}

