parts.text:
{
  "request_id": "4061d17b718f582535a96fdb",
  "rewritten_text": "Good heavens, the Duchess thought, he is just a palm reader after all. How dreadful. I hope he is at least a foreigner; that would make it slightly more acceptable. I must introduce him to you. Introduce him? the Duchess exclaimed. You don't mean he is here? She began searching for her tortoise-shell fan and tattered lace shawl, prepared to leave immediately. Of course he is here; I would never host a party without him. He claims I have a pure psychic hand and that if my thumb were slightly shorter, I would be a confirmed pessimist living in a convent. Oh, I see, the Duchess said, feeling relieved. He tells fortunes, I suppose? And misfortunes, Lady Windermere replied. Plenty of them. Next year, I am in great danger by land and sea, so I plan to live in a balloon and hoist my dinner up in a basket. It is all written on my finger or palm, I forget which. But surely that is tempting Providence, Gladys. My dear Duchess, surely Providence can resist temptation by now. I think everyone should have their palms read monthly to know what to avoid. We do it anyway, but it is pleasant to be warned. If someone doesn't fetch Mr. Podgers, I shall have to go myself. Let me go, Lady Windermere, said a tall, handsome young man standing nearby, listening with an amused smile. Thanks, Lord Arthur, but I fear you wouldn't recognize him. If he is as wonderful as you say, I couldn't miss him. Describe him, and I will bring him to you. He doesn't look like a palmist at all. He isn't mysterious or romantic. He is a short, stout man with a bald head and gold-rimmed spectacles, looking like a cross between a family doctor and a country lawyer. It is not my fault; people are so annoying. My pianists look like poets, and my poets look like pianists. Last season, I invited a dangerous conspirator to dinner—a man who had blown up many people and wore chainmail with a dagger in his sleeve—and he arrived looking like a pleasant clergyman, cracking jokes all evening."
}

