  "rewritten_text": "Were our proud dreams meant to fade like this? We once considered ourselves just below the angels, yet we proved no better than fleeting insects. We called ourselves the finest of creatures, only to find we were merely dust. We complained that the pyramids outlasted their builders, yet even a simple straw hut lasts longer than the entire human race. How can we reconcile this decline with our past ambitions and perceived power? Suddenly, an internal voice spoke clearly: This was decreed from eternity. The forces of time were bound to this outcome since the beginning. Do you wish to reverse the unchangeable laws of necessity? Eternal, unchanging necessity, you who weave the unbreakable chain of events, I will not complain. If my human mind cannot accept that everything is right, I will sit among the ruins and smile, knowing that we were born not to enjoy, but to submit and hope. Would the reader grow tired if I described our long journey from Paris to Geneva in detail? Could I even find the words to express our endless miseries? Patience, reader. Whether you are a spiritual being or a human living on earth, you will read of our extinct race and wonder if we were as fragile as you. We were, so weep for us. Shed tears of compassion, but pay attention to the story of your predecessors. The final events of our journey through France were so horrific that I dare not dwell on them. Every moment holds a painful story that would chill your blood. It is right that I build this record for your instruction, but I will not force you to witness every gruesome detail."
}

