parts.text:
{
  "request_id": "01912125e593730a61e84315",
  "rewritten_text": "Soon his voice called out, asking how much further he had to go. Legrand asked how high he was, and Jupiter replied that he was very high, able to see the sky through the treetops. Legrand told him to ignore the sky and count the limbs he had passed on his side of the trunk. Jupiter counted five. Legrand instructed him to climb one limb higher. Soon, Jupiter announced he had reached the seventh. Legrand, clearly excited, told him to crawl out as far as he could on that limb and report anything unusual. By now, I was convinced of my friend's insanity and worried about getting him home. Jupiter called down, saying he was afraid to venture far because the limb was mostly dead. Legrand asked in a trembling voice if it was truly dead, and Jupiter confirmed it was completely rotten. Legrand expressed great distress, so I intervened, urging him to come home and rest as he had promised. Ignoring me, Legrand asked Jupiter to test the wood with his knife. Jupiter replied that while it was rotten, it might hold his weight if he dropped the heavy bug first. Legrand, suddenly relieved, angrily threatened to break Jupiter's neck if he dropped the beetle. When Jupiter complained about being shouted at, Legrand promised him a silver dollar if he crawled out safely while keeping hold of the insect."
}

