parts.text:
{
  "request_id": "119dd3f22946e5739aeb8fe4",
  "rewritten_text": "When Hiram B. Otis, the American Minister, acquired Canterville Chase, everyone warned him he was acting imprudently, as the estate was undoubtedly haunted. Lord Canterville, a man of impeccable integrity, felt obligated to disclose this when they negotiated the sale. We have avoided living there, Lord Canterville explained, ever since my grandaunt, the Dowager Duchess of Bolton, suffered a permanent breakdown after two skeletal hands touched her shoulders while she dressed. I must inform you that the specter has been witnessed by several relatives and the parish rector, Reverend Augustus Dampier, a Fellow of King’s College. Following the Duchess’s ordeal, our younger staff refused to remain, and Lady Canterville frequently lost sleep due to strange sounds emanating from the library and hallway. My Lord, the Minister replied, I shall accept the furniture and the phantom at an appraised value. I hail from a modern nation where money buys everything; with our energetic youth conquering the Old World and courting your finest performers, I suspect that if a ghost existed in Europe, we would have already secured it for a museum or a traveling exhibit. I believe the ghost is real, Lord Canterville said with a smile, even if it has eluded your enterprising showmen. It has been documented since 1584 and invariably appears before a family death. So does the family physician, Lord Canterville. Regardless, ghosts do not exist, and I doubt the laws of nature are suspended for the British nobility. You are certainly quite natural in America, Lord Canterville replied, failing to grasp the remark, but if you are comfortable with a ghost, that is your affair. Just remember that I provided a warning. Weeks later, the transaction concluded, and after the season ended, the Minister and his family traveled to Canterville Chase. Mrs. Otis, formerly the renowned New York beauty Lucretia R. Tappan of West 53rd Street, was now a striking, middle-aged woman with beautiful eyes and a magnificent profile."
}

