parts.text:
{
  "request_id": "f545e260c3b25fc7a69e2cc1",
  "rewritten_text": "Tom managed to scratch the cupboard with his tool and was planning to work on the bureau when he was called to get ready for Sunday school. Mary gave him a basin of water and soap. He set the basin on a bench outside, dipped the soap, poured the water out, and went inside to wipe his face on the towel. Mary took the towel away and scolded him for not actually washing. Tom felt embarrassed. He tried again, taking a deep breath and scrubbing his face. When he came back inside, he was dripping with soapy water, but his face was only clean up to his chin. Below that line, his skin remained dirty. Mary stepped in and scrubbed him until he was clean, then brushed his wet hair into neat curls. Tom secretly flattened the curls later, as he thought they looked girlish. Mary then brought out his Sunday clothes, which were the only other outfit he owned. She helped him dress, buttoning his jacket, adjusting his large collar, and putting on his straw hat. He looked much better but felt very stiff and miserable in his clean, restrictive clothes. He hoped she would forget his shoes, but she polished them with tallow and brought them out. Frustrated, Tom complained that he was always forced to do things he disliked."
}

