  "request_id": "b73dc30e3f0975cdd703d994",
  "rewritten_text": "Unless you refer to Miss Havisham as a man. And I expect even you would hesitate to claim that. Miss Havisham, in town? Joe asked. Is there any Miss Havisham elsewhere? my sister replied. She desires this boy to visit and play there. Naturally he is going. And he had best play there, my sister added, gesturing for me to appear cheerful and lively, or I shall punish him. I had heard of Miss Havisham in town—everyone for miles around knew of her—as a wealthy, stern woman residing in a vast, gloomy house fortified against thieves, living in total isolation. Well, I never! Joe exclaimed, amazed. I wonder how she came to know Pip! Fool! my sister shouted. Who claimed she knew him? Some person, Joe suggested mildly, mentioned she wanted him to go and play there. Could she not ask Uncle Pumblechook if he knew of a boy to play there? Is it not possible that Uncle Pumblechook is her tenant, and occasionally visits to pay his rent? Could she not then inquire if he knew of a boy? And could Uncle Pumblechook, always thoughtful of us—though you might not realize it, Joseph, she said with deep reproach, as if he were a heartless nephew—then suggest this boy, who stands here prancing—which I certainly was not—that I have always been a devoted slave to? Excellent! Uncle Pumblechook cried. Well stated! Cleverly put! Now Joseph, you understand the situation. No, Joseph, my sister continued reproachfully, while Joe wiped his nose apologetically, you do not yet understand the situation. You may think you do, but you do not, Joseph. You are unaware that Uncle Pumblechook, sensing that this boy’s fortune might be made by visiting Miss Havisham, has offered to drive him to town tonight in his cart, keep him overnight, and escort him to Miss Havisham’s tomorrow morning. Good heavens! my sister cried, tossing aside her bonnet in frustration, here I am speaking to simpletons, while Uncle Pumblechook waits, the horse catches a chill outside, and the boy is covered in soot from head to toe!"
}

