  "rewritten_text": "He had been entirely unaware of his own influence. He followed her into the shrubbery without any plan to test it. Anxious to see how she handled Frank Churchill’s engagement, he arrived with no selfish agenda, hoping only to offer comfort or advice if she allowed it. The rest happened in an instant, driven by his immediate reaction to her words. The delightful realization that she felt nothing for Frank Churchill and that her heart was free sparked the hope that he might eventually win her affection. He had not expected immediate success; in a moment where eagerness overcame judgment, he only wanted her permission to try to win her over. The greater hopes that soon emerged were all the more enchanting. The love he had hoped to cultivate was already his. In half an hour, he had moved from deep distress to something indistinguishable from perfect happiness. Her transformation was just as profound. This brief time gave them both the precious certainty of being loved, clearing away their mutual ignorance, jealousy, and distrust. He had long been jealous, dating back to the arrival or even the anticipation of Frank Churchill. His love for Emma and his jealousy of Churchill had grown together, each emotion revealing the other. It was this jealousy that had driven him to leave the area; the Box Hill outing convinced him to go. He wanted to avoid witnessing such encouraged flirtations and hoped to learn indifference. However, he went to the wrong place. His brother’s home was filled with domestic happiness, and the women there were too amiable. Isabella reminded him so much of Emma—though lacking her brilliance—that he could not move on. He stayed stubbornly until the morning mail brought news of Jane Fairfax. Feeling a relief he did not hesitate to embrace, as he never believed Churchill deserved Emma, his concern for her became too intense to ignore. He rode home through the rain and walked over immediately after dinner to see how this wonderful woman, perfect despite her flaws, was handling the news."
}

