parts.text:
{
  "request_id": "84bb4c4d3bd9cb73d9f7fce1",
  "rewritten_text": "Were our grand ambitions destined to vanish? We once considered ourselves just below the angels, yet we proved as fleeting as insects. We claimed to be the pinnacle of creation, only to reveal ourselves as mere dust. We lamented that pyramids outlived their creators, yet even a simple shepherd’s hut possesses more permanence than all of humanity. How can we reconcile this decline with our former potential? Suddenly, a clear inner voice spoke: This was decreed from eternity; the forces of time were bound to this outcome since the beginning. Do you seek to reverse the unchangeable laws of necessity? Eternal, unchanging Necessity, weaver of the unbreakable chain of events, I will not complain. If my mind cannot grasp that all is right, I will accept that what must be, is, and sit among the ruins with a smile. We were born not to enjoy, but to submit and hope. Will the reader grow weary if I detail our long journey from Paris to Geneva? Could I possibly record the endless miseries we endured? Patience, reader. Whether you are a spiritual being or a human descendant, you will read of this extinct race and wonder if they were as fragile as you. They were, so weep for them, but listen to their story. The final events in France were so horrific that I dare not dwell on them. Every second held a nightmare that would chill your blood. I must build this monument to our history for your instruction, but I will not force you to witness every gruesome detail of our suffering."
}

