parts.text:
{
  "request_id": "2ecbf50f25d310114bc4469c",
  "rewritten_text": "His manner was intensely stubborn, and \"that cursed bug\" were the only words he spoke throughout our trek. I carried two dark lanterns, while Legrand held the scarab dangling from a piece of whip-cord, swinging it like a magician as he walked. Seeing this clear sign of his mental decline, I nearly wept. I decided to indulge his whim for now, hoping to intervene more effectively later. My attempts to learn the purpose of our journey failed; having convinced me to join him, he refused to discuss anything else, answering my inquiries only with \"we shall see!\" We crossed the island's creek in a skiff and climbed the mainland's high ground, heading northwest through a wild, desolate landscape devoid of human tracks. Legrand moved with purpose, pausing briefly only to check landmarks he had apparently set previously. After two hours, as the sun dipped low, we reached an even bleaker region. It was a plateau near the top of a steep, heavily forested hill, scattered with massive boulders that seemed held in place only by the trees they leaned against. Deep ravines added to the grim atmosphere. The platform we reached was choked with brambles, requiring a scythe to clear. Following Legrand's orders, Jupiter cut a path to the base of a towering tulip-tree. Standing among several oaks, it surpassed them all in the splendor of its leaves, the reach of its limbs, and its overall majestic stature."
}

