parts.text:
{
  "request_id": "91cc83f2e7d1694b222714ca",
  "rewritten_text": "Yet there was something even more flamboyant. He would become a pirate! That was the path! Now his future appeared clear and radiant with incredible brilliance. How his reputation would spread, striking terror into hearts! He envisioned himself sailing the lively waves aboard his sleek, dark-hulled vessel, the Spirit of the Storm, his grim flag hoisted high. At the height of his notoriety, he would return to his village, marching into church tanned and rugged, dressed in a velvet doublet, jack-boots, and a crimson sash, armed with pistols and a weathered cutlass, his plumed hat and skull-and-crossbones flag signaling his arrival. He imagined the thrill of hearing the congregation whisper, \"It is Tom Sawyer the Pirate, the Black Avenger of the Spanish Main!\" It was decided; his life’s work was chosen. He would depart home the following morning to begin. He needed to gather his supplies, so he approached a decaying log and dug beneath it with his knife. Hearing a hollow sound, he performed a solemn ritual: \"What has not arrived, come! What is here, remain!\" He cleared the soil to reveal a small wooden box. Inside sat a single marble. Tom was stunned, scratching his head in confusion. \"Well, that is truly bizarre!\" he muttered. He threw the marble aside, deep in thought. His belief in a childhood superstition had crumbled; he and his friends had always considered this ritual foolproof. The legend claimed that burying a marble with the proper words would cause every lost marble to return to that spot after a fortnight. Since it had failed, his confidence was shattered. He had never known it to fail, conveniently forgetting that he had previously lost the locations of his own buried treasures. After pondering the mystery, he concluded that a witch must have meddled and ruined the spell."
}

