parts.text:
{
  "request_id": "a387e8af20c7730bc61f00ab",
  "rewritten_text": "I regretted Jim’s remark; it diminished him in my eyes. My conscience pricked me so severely that I finally promised it I would row to the bank at dawn and confess. Instantly, I felt relieved and buoyant, my burdens vanished. I scanned the darkness for a light, humming softly, until one appeared. Jim cried out, \"We are safe, Huck! We are safe! Celebrate, for that is surely Cairo!\" I replied, \"I will take the canoe to verify; it might be a mistake.\" He eagerly prepared the boat, placing his coat for my comfort and handing me the paddle. As I departed, he added, \"Soon I will shout for joy, knowing I am a free man because of you, Huck. You are my best and only friend; Jim will never forget this.\" I had been eager to betray him, but his words drained my resolve. I paddled slowly, uncertain of my intentions. When I was fifty yards away, Jim called out, \"There you go, the only white gentleman who ever kept his word to old Jim.\" I felt nauseated, yet insisted to myself that I had to proceed. Just then, a skiff carrying two armed men approached. They stopped, and I followed suit. One asked, \"What is that?\" \"A section of a raft,\" I answered. \"Are you aboard it?\" \"Yes, sir.\" \"Is there anyone else?\" \"Only one man.\" \"Five slaves escaped tonight upstream. Is your companion white or black?\" I hesitated, unable to force the words out. I lacked the courage to speak, and realizing my resolve was failing, I finally lied, \"He is white.\" \"We shall investigate ourselves,\" the man said. \"I wish you would,\" I replied, \"because my father is there, and perhaps you could assist me in towing the raft to the light.\""
}

