  "request_id": "99536b39fa3a2ab0c37e24c6",
  "rewritten_text": "May I pose two inquiries? Monks appeared surprised, noting that answering was his choice. That makes three, Mr. Bumble quipped. Is that your expectation? the matron asked. It is, Monks replied. What is the second? What is your plan for it, and could it be used against me? Never, Monks promised, warning them not to approach. He shoved the table away and lifted a trapdoor near Mr. Bumble, who retreated in haste. Look down, Monks commanded, lowering his lantern. I could have dropped you in earlier if I wished. The matron approached the edge, followed by a curious Mr. Bumble. Below, the rain-swollen river churned against rotting mill pilings. If a body were thrown in, where would it end up? Monks asked. Twelve miles downstream and mangled, Bumble answered, shuddering. Monks attached his packet to a lead weight and dropped it into the dark water, where it vanished instantly. The three breathed easier. Monks shut the trapdoor firmly. If the sea yields its dead, it will keep this trash, he remarked. Our meeting is concluded. Certainly, Mr. Bumble agreed quickly. Keep your silence, Monks warned with a menacing glare."
}

