parts.text:
{
  "request_id": "af0fa36da2ee4e8ed5da2ec4",
  "rewritten_text": "I woke early, managed to slip past my creditors, and hurried to a bookstore. I spent my remaining cash on books about mechanics and astronomy. Once home, I studied them constantly until I felt ready to carry out my plan. Meanwhile, I worked to appease the three creditors who had been bothering me. I finally succeeded by selling some furniture to pay half their debt and promising the rest once I finished a project I invited them to help with. Since they were simple men, they easily agreed. Once things were settled, I secretly sold my remaining property with my wife's help. I also borrowed small amounts of money under various excuses, never worrying about how I would pay it back. With this cash, I bought fine cambric muslin, twine, rubber varnish, a custom wicker basket, and other supplies for a massive balloon. I instructed my wife on how to sew the balloon while I wove the twine into a net and attached the hoop and cords. I also purchased a quadrant, compass, telescope, a modified barometer, and two rare astronomical tools. At night, I transported several large casks, long metal tubes, a specific semi-metal, and a dozen jugs of acid to a secluded spot east of Rotterdam. I planned to create a unique gas that no one else had ever used for this purpose. I would gladly reveal the secret, but it belongs to a man in Nantz, France, who shared it with me under strict conditions."
}

