parts.text:
{
  "request_id": "9e88c1b51049728937cea33b",
  "rewritten_text": "He chose Friday, August 17th, for his appearance, spending the day choosing his outfit: a wide-brimmed hat with a red feather, a ruffled burial shroud, and a rusted dagger. By evening, a fierce rainstorm rattled the house, creating the perfect atmosphere for his plans. He intended to sneak into Washington Otis’s room, haunt him from the foot of the bed, and stab himself in the throat to the sound of slow music. He held a grudge against Washington for repeatedly cleaning the Canterville bloodstain with detergent. After terrifying the young man, he planned to visit the Minister and his wife, placing a cold hand on her forehead while whispering gruesome secrets to her husband. He was undecided about Virginia, who had always been kind, so he settled on merely groaning from her wardrobe or scratching at her bedsheets. He was determined to punish the twins by sitting on their chests to induce nightmares, then standing between their beds as a frozen, green corpse before revealing his skeletal form as 'Dumb Daniel,' a role he had perfected over the years. At ten-thirty, he heard the family heading to bed. The twins’ laughter delayed him, but by midnight, the house was silent. As the wind howled and the owl cried, he crept out, while the Otis family slept soundly, unaware of the ghost stalking the halls."
}

