parts.text:
{
  "request_id": "0fa8bb0840cd362469570e49",
  "rewritten_text": "In the middle of the gap, I noticed a white object, though I could not initially identify it. After adjusting my telescope, I realized it was a human skull. Upon this realization, I felt confident the mystery was resolved. The instructions regarding the seventh limb and the east side clearly pointed to the skull's location, while the direction to shoot from the left eye of the death's head could only mean one thing for finding buried treasure. I understood that a bullet dropped from that eye would mark a spot, and a straight line drawn from the trunk through that point and extended fifty feet would reveal where the treasure was hidden. I remarked that the plan was clever yet straightforward, and asked what happened after he departed the Bishop's Hotel. He explained that after noting the tree's position, he headed home. Once he left the devil's seat, the circular gap disappeared and could not be seen again from any other vantage point. Jupiter had been shadowing him, worried by his recent distracted behavior, but he managed to sneak away the next morning to locate the tree. After a difficult search, he succeeded, though his valet threatened to punish him upon his return. I suggested that his initial failure to find the treasure was due to Jupiter dropping the beetle through the right eye of the skull instead of the left. He agreed, noting that this minor error of two and a half inches in the initial placement caused the entire fifty-foot line of direction to be significantly misaligned, leading them far from the actual target."
}

