  "rewritten_text": "Knights in heavy armor were slow. With the ground clear of snow and mud, they could manage a seven-mile pace, swapping horses twice to arrive by six. There would be enough daylight to spot the white cloth on my arm, allowing me to take command. We would surround the prison and rescue the king quickly. It would be a dramatic scene, though I would have preferred noon for the added theatrical effect. To improve my odds, I decided to find people I recognized and reveal my identity, potentially solving our problem without the knights. However, I had to be careful. I needed to acquire fine clothing gradually, buying increasingly expensive outfits at distant shops until I reached silk and velvet. I began my plan, but it failed instantly. Turning a corner, I ran into one of our slaves with a watchman. I coughed, and his sharp look suggested he recognized me. I ducked into a shop, pretending to browse while watching them talk and peer through the door. I decided to escape through the back. I told the shopkeeper I was an undercover officer hunting an escaped slave and asked her to tell my partner at the door to move to the end of the alley to intercept the fugitive. Eager to see a notorious criminal, she hurried off to deliver the message."
}

